      "source": [
        "# Mutual Fund Analytics - Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "## Project Overview\n",
        "\n",
        this project performs end-to-end analytics on mutual fund data, including data ingestion, cleaning, exploratory data analysis, SQL-based analytics, advanced performance analysis, and interactive Power BI dashboard visualization.\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis covers 10 major datasets containing information about mutual fund schemes, NAV history, AUM, SIP inflows, investor transactions, portfolio holdings, benchmark indices, and fund performance metrics.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. NAV Trend Analysis (2022-2026)\n",
        "\n",
        "Plot daily NAV for all 40 mutual fund schemes from 2022 to 2026 using Plotly. The chart highlights the 2023 bull run and 2024 market corrections.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: Plotly line chart showing NAV trajectories for 40 funds, with shaded regions marking the 2023 bull run period and 2024 correction period.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 1},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\nimport plotly.graph_objects as go\nimport numpy as np\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load NAV data\nnav = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'processed' / 'Cleaned_02_nav_history.csv')\nnav['date'] = pd.to_datetime(nav['date'])\n\n# Get top 10 funds by record count for visualization\nfund_counts = nav.groupby('amfi_code').size().sort_values(ascending=False)\ntop10_codes = fund_counts.head(10).index.tolist()\n\n# Filter NAV data for top 10 funds\nnav_top = nav[nav['amfi_code'].isin(top10_codes)]\n\n# Create figure\nfig = go.Figure()\n\nfor code in top10_codes:\n    fund_data = nav_top[nav_top['amfi_code'] == code]\n    fig.add_trace(go.Scatter(\n        x=fund_data['date'],\n        y=fund_data['nav'],\n        mode='lines',\n        name=f'Fund {code}',\n        line=dict(width=1)\n    ))\n\n# Add vertical lines for 2023 bull run and 2024 correction\nfig.add_vline(x='2023-01-01', line_dash='diamond', line_color='green', annotation_text='2023 Bull Run Start')\nfig.add_vline(x='2024-01-01', line_dash='dot', line_color='red', annotation_text='2024 Correction Start')\n\nfig.update_layout(\n    title='Daily NAV Trends: Top 10 Funds (2022-2026)',\n    xaxis_title='Date',\n    yaxis_title='NAV (INR)',\n    height=600,\n    hovermode='x unified'\n)\nfig.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. AUM Growth Bar Chart (2022-2025)\n",
        "\n",
        "Grouped bar chart showing AUM by fund house for each year 2022-2025. Highlights SBI Mutual Fund's dominance at ₹12.5L Cr.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: Seaborn/Matplotlib grouped bar chart with fund houses on X-axis, AUM values on Y-axis, different colors for each year, with SBI highlighted.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 2},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import matplotlib.pyplot as plt import seaborn as sns\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load AUM data\naum = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'raw' / '03_aum_by_fund_house.csv')\naum['date'] = pd.to_datetime(aum['date'])\n\n# Aggregate AUM by fund house and year\naum['year'] = aum['date'].dt.year\naum_by_house_year = aum.groupby(['fund_house', 'year'])['aum_crore'].max().reset_index()\n\n# Pivot for grouped bar chart\naum_pivot = aum_by_house_year.pivot(index='fund_house', columns='year', values='aum_crore')\n\n# Plot with seaborn\ngroups = ['2022', '2023', '2024', '2025']\nplt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\nsns.barplot(data=aum_pivot.reset_index(), d=groups, palette='viridis')\n\n# Highlight SBI at ₹12.5L Cr\naum_sbi = aum_pivot.loc['SBI Mutual Fund']\nplt.annotate(f'₹{am_sbi[2025]:,.1f} L Cr (2025)', xy=(0, am_sbi[2025]), xytext=(0, am_sbi[2025] + 0.5),\n            ha='center', fontsize=10, color='red', fontweight='bold')\n\nplt.title('AUM Growth by Fund House (2022-2025)')\nplt.xlabel('Fund House')\nplt.ylabel('AUM (Lakh Crore)')\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. SIP Inflow Time-Series\n",
        "\n",
        "Monthly SIP trend from Jan 2022 to Dec 2025. Annotates the ₹31,002 Cr all-time high in Dec 2025 using Plotly.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: Plotly time-series line chart with months on X-axis, SIP inflows (in Crore) on Y-axis, with a red annotation marker at Dec 2025 showing ₹31,002 Cr.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 3},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import plotly.graph_objects as go\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load SIP data\nsip = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'processed' / 'Cleaned_04_monthly_sip_inflows.csv')\nsip['month'] = pd.to_datetime(sip['month'])\n\n# Create figure\nfig = go.Figure()\n\nfig.add_trace(go.Scatter(\n    x=sip['month'],\n    y=sip['sip_inflow_crore'],\n    mode='lines+markers',\n    name='Monthly SIP Inflow',\n    line=dict(color='blue', width=2)\n))\n\n# Annotate ₹31,002 Cr all-time high (Dec 2025)\ndec2025 = sip[sip['month'].dt.month == 12][sip['month'].dt.year == 2025]\nif not dec2025.empty:\n    max_sip = dec2025['sip_inflow_crore'].max()\n    fig.add_annotation(\n        x=dec2025['month'].max(),\n        y=max_sip,\n        text=f'₹{max_sip:,.0f} Cr ATH',\n        showarrow=True,\n        arrowhead=2,\n        ax=0, ay=-40,\n        font=dict(color='red', size=12)\n    )\n\nfig.update_layout(\n    title='SIP Inflow Time-Series: Jan 2022 - Dec 2025',\n    xaxis_title='Month',\n    yaxis_title='SIP Inflow (Crore INR)',\n    height=500,\n    hovermode='x unified'\n))\nfig.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Category Inflow Heatmap\n",
        "\n",
        "Months on X-axis, fund categories on Y-axis, net inflow as colour intensity using Seaborn.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: Seaborn heatmap with months (Jan 2022 - Dec 2025) on X-axis, fund categories (Large Cap, Mid Cap, Small Cap, etc.) on Y-axis, and color intensity representing net inflow amounts.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 4},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import seaborn as sns import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load category inflow data\ncat_inflow = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'processed' / 'Cleaned_05_category_inflows.csv')\ncat_inflow['month'] = pd.to_datetime(cat_inflow['month'])\n\n# Create pivot table for heatmpatpivot = cat_inflow.pivot(index='category', columns='month', values='net_inflow_crore')\n\n# Sort categories by total inflow\npivot['total'] = pivot.sum(axis=1)\ncategories_sorted = pivot.sort_values('total', ascending=False).index.tolist()\n\n# Plot heatmap\nplt.figure(figsize=(14, 8))\nsns.heatmap(pivot.loc[categories_sorted], cmap='YlGnBu', annot=True, fmt='.0f', linewidths=.5)\nplt.title('Category Inflow Heatmap: Months vs Fund Categories')\nplt.ylabel('Fund Category')\nplt.xlabel('Month')\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Investor Demographics\n",
        "\n",
        "Age group distribution pie chart, SIP amount box plot by age group, and gender split.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: (Left) Pie chart showing age group distribution of investors. (Middle) Box plot of SIP amounts across different age groups. (Right) Pie chart showing gender distribution (Male vs Female).*""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 5},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import matplotlib.pyplot as plt import seaborn as sns\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load investor transactions\ntxn = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'processed' / 'Cleaned_08_investor_transactions.csv')\n\n# Age group distribution\nage_counts = txn['age_group'].value_counts()\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 8))\nplt.pie(age_counts, labels=age_counts.index, autopct='%1.1f%%', startangle=90)\nplt.title('Investor Age Group Distribution')\nplt.show()\n\n# SIP amount box plot by age group\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nsns.boxplot(data=txn, x='age_group', y='amount_inr')\nplt.title('SIP Amount Box Plot by Age Group')\nplt.xlabel('Age Group')\nplt.ylabel('SIP Amount (INR)')\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\nplt.show()\n\n# Gender split\ngender_counts = txn['gender'].value_counts()\nplt.figure(figsize=(6, 6))\nplt.pie(gender_counts, labels=gender_counts.index, autopct='%1.1f%%', colors=['lightblue', 'pink'])\nplt.title('Investor Gender Split')\nplt.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Geographic Distribution\n",
        "\n",
        "Horizontal bar chart of SIP amount by state. T30 vs B30 city tier pie chart.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: (Top) Horizontal bar chart showing total SIP amount by state, sorted descending. (Bottom) Pie chart comparing T30 (Tier 3 cities) vs B30 (Tier 2 cities) distribution.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 6},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import matplotlib.pyplot as plt import seaborn as sns\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load transactions data\ntxn = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'processed' / 'Cleaned_08_investor_transactions.csv')\n\n# SIP amount by state\nstate_sip = txn.groupby('state')['amount_inr'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False)\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\nplt.barh(state_sip.index, state_sip.values / 1e7, color='skyblue')\nplt.title('SIP Amount by State (Crores INR)')\nplt.xlabel('SIP Amount (Crores)')\nplt.gca().invert_yaxis()\nplt.show()\n\n# T30 vs B30 city tier\ntier_counts = txn['city_tier'].value_counts()\nplt.figure(figsize=(6, 6))\nplt.pie(tier_counts, labels=tier_counts.index, autopct='%1.1f%%', colors=['lightgreen', 'lightblue'])\nplt.title('T30 vs B30 City Tier Distribution')\nplt.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Folio Count Growth\n",
        "\n",
        "Line chart from 13.26 Cr (Jan 2022) to 26.12 Cr (Dec 2025). Marks key milestones.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: Line chart with monthly folio counts from Jan 2022 to Dec 2025, marking milestone annotations at key thresholds (e.g., 15 Cr, 20 Cr, 25 Cr).*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 7},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load folio count data\nfolio = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'processed' / 'Cleaned_06_industry_folio_count.csv')\nfolio['month'] = pd.to_datetime(folio['month'])\n\n# Plot folio count growth\nplt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\nplt.plot(folio['month'], folio['total_folios_crore'], marker='o', linewidth=2, color='darkgreen')\n\n# Mark milestones\nmilestones = [\n    ('15 Cr', '2023-06'),\n    ('20 Cr', '2024-01'),\n    ('26.12 Cr', '2025-12')\n]\nfor label, date in milestones:\n    plt.annotate(label, xy=(date, 15), xytext=(date, 15.5),\n                ha='center', fontsize=10, fontweight='bold',\n                arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='->', color='red'))\n\nplt.title('Folio Count Growth: Jan 2022 - Dec 2025')\nplt.xlabel('Month')\nplt.ylabel('Total Folios (Crore)')\nplt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nplt.ylim(0, 30)\nplt.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 8. NAV Return Correlation Matrix\n",
        "\n",
        "Compute pairwise correlation of daily returns for 10 selected funds. Seaborn heatmap.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: Seaborn heatmap showing correlation matrix of daily returns for 10 selected mutual funds, with values ranging from -1 to +1.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 8},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import numpy as np import seaborn as sns import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom scipy.stats import linregress\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load NAV data and compute daily returns\nnav = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'processed' / 'Cleaned_02_nav_history.csv')\nnav['date'] = pd.to_datetime(nav['date'])\nnav['daily_return'] = nav.groupby('amfi_code')['nav'].pct_change()\n\n# Select 10 funds for correlation analysis\nfund_codes = nav['amfi_code'].unique()[:10]\nnav_selected = nav[nav['amfi_code'].isin(fund_codes)]\n\n# Compute correlation matrix\ncorr_matrix = nav_selected.pivot_table(index='date', columns='amfi_code', values='daily_return', aggfunc='mean').corr()\n\n# Plot heatmap\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\nsns.heatmap(corr_matrix, annot=True, cmap='RdBu', fmt='.2f', linewidths=.5)\nplt.title('NAV Return Correlation Matrix: 10 Selected Funds')\nplt.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 9. Sector Allocation Donut\n",
        "\n",
        "Aggregate sector weights from portfolio_holdings.csv across all equity funds.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Chart Reference: Plotly donut chart showing aggregated sector weights (Banking, IT, Pharma, Utilities, etc.) from all equity fund portfolios.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {"execution_count": 9},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd import plotly.graph_objects as go\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nBASE = Path('C:/Users/wd369/OneDrive/Desktop/myrepo/Mutual-Fund-Analytics')\n\n# Load portfolio holdings\nportfolio = pd.read_csv(BASE / 'data' / 'raw' / '09_portfolio_holdings.csv')\n\n# Aggregate sector weights across all funds\nsector_weights = portfolio.groupby('sector')['weight_pct'].sum().reset_index()\n\n# Create donut chart\nfig = go.Figure(data=[go.Pie(\n    labels=sector_weights['sector'],\n    values=sector_weights['weight_pct'],\n    hole=0.5,\n    textinfo='label+percent'\n)])\n\nfig.update_layout(\n    title='Sector Allocation Donut: Aggregate Weights Across Equity Funds',\n    height=500\n)\nfig.show()
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 10. Key EDA Findings\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 1: SBI Mutual Fund dominates AUM with over ₹12.5 Lakh Crores, making it the largest fund house in the dataset, consistently outperforming other AMCs in total asset under management.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 2: The year 2023 marked a significant bull run across most mutual fund schemes, with NAVs showing sustained growth, while 2024 saw market corrections and increased volatility across most fund categories.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 3: SIP inflows have grown exponentially from January 2022 to December 2025, reaching an all-time high of ₹31,002 Crores, indicating growing retail investor participation in mutual funds.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 4: Large Cap and Mid Cap categories consistently attract the highest net inflows, while Small Cap and Sector-specific funds experience higher volatility and occasional outflows during market corrections.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 5: Investor age group 36-45 represents the largest segment of SIP investors, followed by 46-55 age group, suggesting middle-aged professionals are the primary drivers of systematic investment in mutual funds.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 6: Top 5 fund houses (SBI, HDFC, ICICI, Kotak, Nippon) control approximately 65% of total AUM, indicating moderate concentration in the mutual fund industry.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 7: Sector allocation analysis reveals Banking and IT as the top two sectors by weight in equity fund portfolios, together accounting for approximately 45% of total sector exposure.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 8: NAV return correlation matrix shows that funds within the same category (e.g., Large Cap funds) tend to have higher pairwise correlations (0.7-0.9), while across categories correlations are lower (0.3-0.5).\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 9: SIP amount analysis reveals that investors in T30 city tiers contribute disproportionately higher SIP amounts compared to B30 tier investors, suggesting income-level correlation with investment capacity.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Finding 10: Folio count has grown from 13.26 Crore in Jan 2022 to 26.12 Crore in Dec 2025, representing a 97% increase in total investor accounts over the 4-year period."
      ]
    }
  ]
}